downloads = page('Download Wood.', 'Install the game companion, then use the dedicated packager to build icon-ready TUNG mods.', f'''<div class="downloadbox"><span class="tag">Windows x64 · Wood 2.3.0</span><h2>Wood Setup</h2><p>Installs the UE4SS runtime, in-game mod menu, included mods, uninstaller, and Wood Launcher.</p><div class="meta"><span>{size}</span><span>Offline installation</span><span>Windows x64</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="downloads/WoodSetup.exe" download>Download Wood Setup ↓</a><a class="btn secondary" href="guides.html">Installation guide</a></div><p class="micro">Unsigned executable; Windows may show an unknown-publisher prompt. SHA-256: <code>{checksum}</code></p></div><div class="downloadbox" style="margin-top:18px"><span class="tag">Standalone companion</span><h2>Wood Launcher</h2><p>A small Steam shortcut. When TUNG starts, the installed UE4SS proxy loads Wood into the game.</p><div class="meta"><span>{launcher_size}</span><span>Windows x64</span><span>Works with installed Wood Setup</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="downloads/WoodLauncher.exe" download>Download Wood Launcher ↓</a></div><p class="micro">SHA-256: <code>{launcher_checksum}</code></p></div><div class="downloadbox" style="margin-top:18px"><span class="tag">Windows x64 · Mod authoring</span><h2>Wood Mod Packager</h2><p>Bundle a Lua mod, optional PNG icon, and mod details into one <code>.tungmod</code> file that Wood loads from the game’s Mods folder.</p><div class="meta"><span>{packager.stat().st_size / 1024 / 1024:.1f} MB</span><span>PNG up to 2048×2048</span><span>No Python install needed</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="downloads/WoodModPackager.exe" download>Download Mod Packager ↓</a></div><p class="micro">Unsigned executable. SHA-256: <code>{packager_checksum}</code></p></div><h2>Build and install a mod package</h2><ol><li>Run <code>WoodModPackager.exe</code> and choose your mod’s <code>.lua</code> source.</li><li>Enter a unique mod ID, name, version, author, and description. Add a PNG icon if wanted, then choose where to save the package.</li><li>Click <strong>Build .tungmod</strong>. The tool creates one package containing the Lua, metadata, and optional icon.</li><li>Copy the resulting <code>.tungmod</code> into TUNG’s <code>Mods</code> folder and restart TUNG. The F10 mod list displays its PNG icon when the image can be loaded.</li></ol><h2>Install Wood</h2><ol><li>Download and run Wood Setup. Choose the TUNG folder when prompted.</li><li>Run TUNG through Steam and press <kbd>F10</kbd> to open Wood’s mod menu.</li></ol><p>To verify downloaded executables, compare their displayed SHA-256 with <a href="downloads/SHA256SUMS.txt" download>SHA256SUMS.txt</a>.</p><h2>Compatibility</h2><p>Windows x64 and the current Steam installation of TUNG. Game updates can require a Wood runtime update.</p>''')
